## 1:35–2:10 — API demo

**Visual:** One simple and one ambiguous synthetic incident through the OpenAI-compatible endpoint.

"The submitted endpoint serves the measured strong-only profile. It overrides even a client's
weaker response-format request with the exact strict triage schema used in the benchmark, then
validates tool arguments, safety, and internal consistency. Invalid upstream output fails closed
with HTTP 502 and is never forwarded. Every tool is a deterministic read-only fixture, and model
text never reaches a shell. Weak/strong A4 routing remains a future option only if calibration and
the complete held-out gate approve it."

## 2:10–2:38 — Reusability and auditability

**Visual:** `optimized-profile.yaml`, `claims.json`, attested release bundle, reproduction command.

“Replace the incident cases with another objectively scored agent workload and reuse the same
pipeline. The repository carries sanitized formal rows and exact claim IDs; the attested release
adds the full redacted raw requests, commands, logs, hashes, and integrity receipts.”

